    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 56 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the derived `timezone` field on the owner response, mapping locality/region \u2192 IANA timezone via the fixed table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane).\n\nChanges:\n- **`mapper/Timezone.java`** (new) \u2014 helper mirroring the existing `Locality`/`ContactPreference` pattern. It reads the owner's region via `Locality.of(owner)` (so timezone always agrees with the reported `locality`) and looks it up in the fixed region\u2192timezone table; returns `null` for regions with no entry (e.g. `UNKNOWN`), leaving the field absent.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", ...)` expression alongside the other derived fields.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `timezone` string property to the `OwnerDto` schema (documenting the table and the absent-when-unknown behavior), which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the getter/setter.\n\nThe new `Cp42Tests` (asserts `timezone` = `Australia/Sydney` for a Sydney/NSW owner) passes, and all pre-existing tests remain green.",
